Z||000000||jlhuber||01-29-2000||11:58 PM||||FYI...  i don't know if anyone has tried them yet, but if you are looking for parts here is a place to try. their ad in the yellow pages reads:<BR>        <BR>        INTERNATIONAL PARTS<BR>       any part, any vehicle, <BR>        used, rebuilt, new.  <BR>specializing in eng's, trans, ecu's <BR>       warranty on all parts <BR>       <A HREF="http://www.easyfindparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.easyfindparts.com</A>   <BR>       toll free 800-825-3121.  <P>in my opinion they kinda beat around the bush a little, but if someone is in need of a part, it's worth a shot.  ||||reg||4
Z||000001||terryk||01-30-2000||01:27 AM||||A good GM dealer is Gold Rush Chevrolet in Auburn California. They will ship anywhere UPS. (530) 885-0471.<P>Their list prices are usually less than the other places discount prices. They will also spend the time to find parts and look up parts that many other dealers say are out of production. I've bought many parts people here have not been able to get.<P>Always worth a try.<BR>No, I don't work for them!||||reg||1
